      "message": "[Critical] Line 146: This synchronizes using the raw `peerId` from the push payload. In the call push flow, peer identifiers are often transported in the same external format used by call signaling, which can include a `ring:`/`jami:` scheme or otherwise differ from the normalized URI used by conversation membership. Passing the unnormalized value can make `syncConversationsWith` a no-op, so the incoming call still may not be delivered. Normalize the peer id with the same helper/path used elsewhere before syncing, and only sync if normalization succeeds.\n```suggestion\nlet normalizedPeerId \u003d JamiURI(schema: URIType.ring, infoHach: peerId).uriString\nself.conversationService.syncConversationsWith(uri: normalizedPeerId, accountId: accountId)\n```",
